<title>AUSTRALIA: Australian stocks seen maintaining positive tone.</title>
<headline>Australian stocks seen maintaining positive tone.</headline>
<text>
<p>-----------------(Snapshot 9.10 a.m./2310 GMT)-----------------</p>
<p>AORD cl	    2625.7   +15.2   DJIA cl	7289.41   -41.63</p>
<p>SPI Sycom cl     2626.0    -9.0   US 30yr cl	6.90    -0.02</p>
<p>10yrbond futs    92.630  +0.200   Gold NY 343.50 Lon fix 343.90</p>
<p>AUD     $0.7576 (Mon   $0.7582)   CRB Index cl  248.64    -2.32</p>
<p>NIKKEI cl	20451.85 +383.04   FTSE cl	 4562.8    -58.5</p>
<p>S&amp;P500(Globex)   845.60   -0.60   NZSE40 open  2343.73   -13.07</p>
<p>--------------------------(June 3)-----------------------------</p>
<p>*Stocks expected to hold positive tone despite fall in U.S. blue chip stocks. &quot;Resources should continue to be strong on the lower interest rates,&quot; said a Brisbane-based broker.</p>
<p>*Pre-open bids A$19.00 (-.15), A$18.75 (-.05), A$5.90 (+.01), A$8.33  (+.003)</p>
<p>*Dow industrials finish lower after mixed session in which small-cap stocks gain at expense of blue-chips</p>
<p>*ADRs:News Corp  NWS.N 17-5/8 (-1/8), BHP 29-3/8 (+1/2), WMC 25-1/2 (-1/2), National Australia Bank 71-3/4 (+1/4)</p>
<p>*Gold price eased in low volumes, copper prices led most base metals to lower closes on speculative selling and technical pressure.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
